        1017,
        1821,
        1374
      ],
      "category": "List-item",
      "text": "2. The City Rent Administrator may appoint three deputies and may determine their relative rank. The Administrator shall assign to such deputies their duties, and may, by instrument in writing filed in the City Rent Agency, designate any deputy or other officer or employee of such Agency to possess any of his powers and perform such of his duties, and for such time and under such conditions, as he may specify. During a vacancy in the office of the Administrator, or whenever by reason of illness or absence from the City he shall be prevented from attending to the duties of his office, the highest ranking deputy not absent or under disability shall act as the head of such Agency.",
